  "final_message": "**Status: reproduced.** The bug shows up on this checkout (3.5.17, commit a9269c6). I made no production code changes.\n\n**Command** (from the repo root, also saved in `out/run_command.txt`):\n\n```\nnpx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlot.spec.ts\n```\n\nIt exits 1 now. It should exit 0 once the bug is fixed.\n\n**What I saw**\n- The test `renders the <template> content (names: _slot1/_slot2)` fails:\n  - Expected `<section>H<div>one|two</div></section>`.\n  - Received `<section>H<div>fallback1|fallback2</div></section>`.\n  - The `<template #_slot1>` and `<template #_slot2>` content is dropped and the `<slot>` fallback content renders instead, which is what the report describes.\n- The shape is the one from the report:\n  - `BaseLayout` is used with a conditional `<template v-if=\"show\" #header>`.\n  - `SubComponent` sits next to it, with `<template #_slot1>` and `<template #_slot2>` filling its `<slot name=\"_slot1\">` and `<slot name=\"_slot2\">`.\n- Two controls in the same file pass:\n  - The same markup with names `slot1` and `slot2` (no underscore) renders `one|two`.\n  - The underscore names without the `v-if` sibling also render `one|two`.\n- I also ran the same scenario against published builds (`vue.cjs.js` in jsdom, scratch script in `/tmp`). Both outputs are rendered fully, in the order shown.\n\n| Version | Underscore names | Plain names |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3.5.13 | `one\\|two` | `one\\|two` |\n| 3.5.14 | `default1\\|default2` | `one\\|two` |\n| 3.5.17 | `default1\\|default2` | `one\\|two` |\n\n  This matches the reported regression window.\n- The compiled render code is identical in structure for `_slot1` and `slot1` (checked on this checkout's compiler). The difference is at runtime, not in the compiler output.\n\n**Caveats**\n- I built the scenario from the written conditions in the report, not from the playground project. I tried to decode the playground link but that was blocked, so I did not use it. The exact `BaseLayout.vue` and `SubComponent.vue` contents may differ from mine.\n- The templates are compiled at runtime from strings in jsdom, not from `.vue` SFC files.\n- It is deterministic, with the same result on every run.\n- I did not investigate the cause.\n\n**File:** `/work/runs/91c4c93233/repo/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlot.spec.ts` (new, untracked).\n",
  "run_command": "npx vitest run --project unit packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlot.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlot.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlot.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..0dee5d8\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlot.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\n+import { createApp, ref } from '../src'\n+\n+// Reproduction for: \"Slot <template> not working when its name starts with an\n+// underscore (_) since v3.5.14\".\n+//\n+// Shape from the report: SubComponent declares <slot>s with fallback content and\n+// is used (with <template #_name> content) inside BaseLayout, as a sibling of a\n+// conditionally rendered <template v-if #slot> of BaseLayout.\n+describe('slot <template> whose name starts with an underscore', () => {\n+  const BaseLayout = {\n+    template: `<section><slot name=\"header\">header-fallback</slot><slot /></section>`,\n+  }\n+\n+  function mountWith(sub: string, usage: string) {\n+    const SubComponent = {\n+      template: `<div><slot name=\"${sub}1\">fallback1</slot>|<slot name=\"${sub}2\">fallback2</slot></div>`,\n+    }\n+    const container = document.createElement('div')\n+    createApp({\n+      components: { BaseLayout, SubComponent },\n+      setup: () => ({ show: ref(true) }),\n+      template: usage,\n+    }).mount(container)\n+    return container.innerHTML\n+  }\n+\n+  const usageWith = (prefix: string, withVIfSibling = true) => `\n+    <BaseLayout>\n+      ${withVIfSibling ? `<template v-if=\"show\" #header>H</template>` : ``}\n+      <SubComponent>\n+        <template #${prefix}1>one</template>\n+        <template #${prefix}2>two</template>\n+      </SubComponent>\n+    </BaseLayout>`\n+\n+  // The reported bug: the <template> content must be rendered instead of the\n+  // slot's default (fallback) content. Fails on this checkout and on v3.5.14+,\n+  // passes on v3.5.13.\n+  it('renders the <template> content (names: _slot1/_slot2)', () => {\n+    expect(mountWith('_slot', usageWith('_slot'))).toBe(\n+      `<section>H<div>one|two</div></section>`,\n+    )\n+  })\n+\n+  // Controls (same input without the trigger) -- these pass today.\n+  it('control: same markup with names slot1/slot2 (no underscore)', () => {\n+    expect(mountWith('slot', usageWith('slot'))).toBe(\n+      `<section>H<div>one|two</div></section>`,\n+    )\n+  })\n+\n+  it('control: underscore names without the conditional <template v-if> sibling', () => {\n+    expect(mountWith('_slot', usageWith('_slot', false))).toBe(\n+      `<section>header-fallback<div>one|two</div></section>`,\n+    )\n+  })\n+})\n"
